    "text": "To determine the combined length of the CDs that James buys, we need to calculate the length of each CD and then sum them up.\n\n1. Identify the length of the first two CDs:\n   Each of the first two CDs is 1.5 hours long. Therefore, the total length of the first two CDs is:\n   \\[\n   1.5 \\text{ hours} + 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n2. Identify the length of the third CD:\n   The third CD is twice as long as one of the first two CDs. Since each of the first two CDs is 1.5 hours long, the third CD is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the combined length of all three CDs:\n   Add the lengths of the first two CDs and the third CD:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} = 9 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the combined length of the CDs is \\(\\boxed{9}\\) hours.",
